      "description": "Playing a basic Island on turn 2 instead of a tapped dual land wastes an opportunity. With only 1 land in play (presumably from turn 1), playing a tapped land like Meticulous Archive now would let it enter untapped-equivalent by turn 3 while also providing a surveil trigger. The Island provides no extra value. Since the player has No More Lies (WU) and Three Steps Ahead (U) as potential turn 2-3 plays, they want WU available on turn 3. Playing Meticulous Archive (Plains/Island) tapped now gives access to W and U on turn 3 alongside turn 1's land, enabling No More Lies. Playing Island now means they'd need to play Hallowed Fountain (paying 2 life) or another dual untapped on turn 3 to have WU available. Meticulous Archive also provides a surveil to potentially set up draws.",
