    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Discarding Ardyn, the Usurper as the additional cost for Bitter Triumph targeting their own Superior Spider-Man. While the discard choice itself is defensible (Ardyn costs 5BBB and is extremely hard to cast), the broader play of using Bitter Triumph to destroy your own creature is highly suspect - it's a 2-for-1 against yourself (spending Bitter Triumph + discarding Ardyn) for no clear benefit. There's already an Ardyn in the graveyard, so the second copy could have some marginal graveyard value, but the cost is enormous.",
