    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Tishana's Tidebinder in precombat main phase before playing the Restless Anchorage land. Lands should be played before spells as a general sequencing principle - it's free and keeps options open. Additionally, Tidebinder has flash and could be held up alongside counterspells to react to opponent's plays, which is especially relevant at 2 life where every decision matters.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Tishana's Tidebinder before playing Restless Anchorage land",
      "better_line": "Play Restless Anchorage first, then consider whether to deploy Tidebinder now or hold it with flash alongside No More Lies and Spell Snare for the opponent's turn, maintaining maximum flexibility at 2 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 199,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 238,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 2 life with Tishana's Tidebinder (3/2 flash) on the stack, activating Restless Anchorage now makes it a creature only until end of THIS turn - it won't be available as a blocker during the opponent's next combat. Meanwhile, No More Lies would either counter the Tidebinder (if opponent can't pay 3) or at minimum tax 3 mana from the opponent. Letting a 3/2 resolve when at 2 life without attempting to counter it is potentially game-losing.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Restless Anchorage to become a 2/3 creature until end of turn (useless since it's Libby's turn and won't persist to block)",
      "better_line": "Cast No More Lies targeting Tishana's Tidebinder to either counter it or force the opponent to pay 3 additional mana, preserving Restless Anchorage activation for blocking on the opponent's combat step",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 200,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 239,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "GPT4om Timmy used Awaken the Honored Dead's Chapter I destroy ability to target itself, completely wasting the card for no effect. The opponent is at 2 life and has Rest in Peace (which shuts down graveyard strategies), Seam Rip (which is exiling one of Timmy's permanents), and Tishana's Tidebinder on the battlefield. Any of these would have been a meaningful target. Rest in Peace is particularly devastating as it exiles all cards that would go to graveyards, neutering Timmy's entire game plan. Tishana's Tidebinder is a 3/2 creature that could block or attack. Seam Rip is exiling something. Instead, Timmy destroyed their own saga for zero value.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Awaken the Honored Dead (itself) with its own Chapter I destroy ability, destroying it for no benefit.",
      "better_line": "Destroy Rest in Peace to re-enable graveyard strategies, or destroy Tishana's Tidebinder to remove a creature threat, or destroy Seam Rip to get back the exiled permanent. With the opponent at 2 life, removing Tidebinder (a blocker/attacker) or Rest in Peace (to unlock graveyard recursion for future turns) would have been far superior.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 206,
      "player": "GPT4om Timmy",
      "decision_index": 245,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Grok4F Libby is at 2 life and their opponent cast Bitter Triumph targeting Tishana's Tidebinder. Libby has Spell Snare in hand, which counters spells with mana value 2 — Bitter Triumph costs {1}{B} and has mana value 2, making it a valid target. Libby also has No More Lies available. By not countering Bitter Triumph, Libby loses Tishana's Tidebinder, which was likely locking down something important (possibly Overlord of the Balemurk). At 2 life with the opponent also at 2, losing a key creature and potentially unlocking an opponent's threat is devastating. Either Spell Snare (free, costs only {U}) or No More Lies would have saved the Tidebinder.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Bitter Triumph, allowing Tishana's Tidebinder to be destroyed.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Bitter Triumph (mana value 2) to counter it and keep Tishana's Tidebinder alive.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 218,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 258,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 2 life each with no opponent creatures on board, Restless Anchorage would provide a lethal attacker next turn (2/3 flyer for {1}{W}{U}) while still allowing countermagic backup. Cori Mountain Monastery provides red mana that doesn't support any cards in hand and delays the win condition by a turn.",
      "action_taken": "Played Cori Mountain Monastery, which provides red mana and an expensive card exile ability neither of which are relevant to the current hand or game state.",
      "better_line": "Play Restless Anchorage to set up lethal next turn by activating it as a 2/3 flyer, attacking for 2 damage at the opponent's 2 life, while holding up Spell Snare or No More Lies for protection.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 229,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 267,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Cast Day of Judgment with zero creatures on either side of the battlefield, accomplishing nothing and wasting a card. The opponent is at 2 life with no creatures, and Restless Anchorage was available as a land drop that becomes a 2/3 flyer — which would attack for lethal next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Day of Judgment destroying zero creatures.",
      "better_line": "Play Restless Anchorage, hold up No More Lies and Spell Snare for countermagic protection, then animate Restless Anchorage next turn and attack for 2 damage to win the game.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 230,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 268,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 2 life each in a control mirror with only counterspells in hand, Libby declined to play Restless Anchorage - a creature land that serves as a win condition. Both players are at 2 life, and Restless Anchorage can become a 2/3 flyer to attack for lethal. Since it enters tapped, playing it in postcombat main has zero downside - it doesn't reduce available mana for counterspells this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to play any land, missing the land drop entirely.",
      "better_line": "Play Restless Anchorage in postcombat main. It enters tapped with no mana cost, provides an additional mana source next turn, and more importantly serves as a creature-land win condition that can attack for lethal in a game where both players are at 2 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 233,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 271,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Jeskai Revelation is on the stack and can deal 4 damage to Libby who is at 2 life. Not countering it with No More Lies allows a lethal spell to resolve. Even if the opponent could pay the {3} tax, Libby should attempt the counter since dying is the alternative.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting No More Lies, allowing Jeskai Revelation to resolve.",
      "better_line": "Cast No More Lies targeting Jeskai Revelation to counter it unless opponent pays {3}. With 8 lands, opponent may be able to pay, but it's the only way to potentially survive.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 252,
      "player": "Grok4F Libby",
      "decision_index": 285,
    }
  ],
